---
tags:
  - Half-Elf
date: 2026-03-23T00:00:00-04:00
---

Johnny Skyfall is a half-elf man in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], friendly and profane, who wears dark glasses and a jean jacket. He has died before and been brought back several times, and keeps a black chess piece on a necklace through which he speaks to a [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Ghost]] named Red.

He was killed with [[People/Benny|Benny]] and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] in the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and came back by way of [[Aut]], leaving a piece of himself in the [[Pharos]].

[[Aut]] later called the piece of him left in the Pharos back into him, and he was whole again. He faced the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], who had helped kill him, in a Widdershins alley, and saw him dead.

Johnny brought Hlarf's bank card to [[Smiler]] at [[Org/The Undertable/index|the Undertable]], who drew nine hundred gold from it and kept fifty for the work.

He spoke to the [[Gas-n-Go Heart|Heart]] in the obsidian at the fane's center and convinced it that Tywelwyn had struck first and that the Party owned it now. From Tywelwyn's wardrobe he took a black robe whose sleeves hold far more than they should, and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s business cards.

At the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]] he spun the Party's account of the fane and the radar dishes to [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/People/Inquisitor Penitence|Penitence]], leaving out the cards, their deaths, [[Aut]] and the invitation, while the room's bell rang for everything true they said.

When they forced [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Brooks]]'s flat, he threw silver needle darts at the empty air by the window and brought the fight on. He put an albatross and a song on the [[Bestiary/Cairn White|cairn white]] and frightened it, and the [[Bestiary/Lovelorn|lovelorn]] knocked him down. He also kicked in [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]]'s door to announce he had won the gang war and asked him to fence the gang's two cars. He drank until sunrise and told whoever was watching that he knew they were there.

He gave the name Jonathan Skyfall at the parking-lot sale and talked the [[Org/Velvet Mark/index|Velvet Mark]] through the minivan's history, tip-tapping his drum while he did. Back at the bar he had a stolen suit tailored and added a shoulder perch for a bird, spoke to [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Red]] through his pond piece to arrange a word with Donnie, and drank coffee to stay awake. At the cabin he told Anaïs who the Party were and that Aut had marked them, and the shackle opened at his touch.

Before the pilgrimage he spent his days at the [[Sin and Tonic]] helping the [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] members with their work, looking to make himself useful to the group.

On the road to the gathering he spotted the ambush at a rest-stop gas station: fresh tire tracks to a white van, no footprints leading from it, and a glint of a scope inside. He threw up an illusion of a one-way mirror around the van, and when the robbers came out he yelled warnings. The best-dressed of them, a masked man with a strange pistol, saw through the illusion and shot him, and another put a slug through his chest with a long gun. He questioned the one robber they took alive, who said the crew had bought their guns from a man named Lark in a [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] neighborhood called [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]].

At the pilgrimage he took a two-faced theater mask, put his dark glasses on over it, and played music as the four of them walked onto the main street. He stayed in the fortune teller's line with [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] only long enough to send word to the others that the far path led to gladiator combat, and then went to the train yard.

When the red wheel summoned three [[Bestiary/Barbazu|Barbazu]] and a [[Bestiary/Brimorak|Brimorak]], he traded insults with one devil until it was shaken, tried to frighten all three, and put a burning word of praise on the brimorak to set it up for his friends. It went badly. [[People/Benny|Benny]] went down, and Johnny, prone and trying to heal him, was struck down before the spell took; he woke again to the sound of his own music and healed Benny back to his feet. He was one of the two who ended the night on the ground with a wound that would not close.

At the pilgrimage he drew the three dots of [[Aut]]'s mark on a notebook page and laid it in the overlap between himself and Benny, which the association machine could not read but accepted anyway, and took the dice table with Benny. He called [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Red]] through his chess piece and learned their contact at [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] is [[Org/Sable and Suns/People/Lark Crowe|Lark Crowe]], and that the arms dealer [[People/Moonlight|Moonlight]] sells in the market in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]]. At the Vane manor he introduced himself as Dave Fuller and said he was a great admirer of Arctos, and spent the wait sulking rather than give his real name.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]] he spent about three hours with [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] going through the periodicals on cults and the [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]]. He found the oldest mention of the Embercall in the first reports of the wall of fire around [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], and a newspaper clipping about a five-man fan club of Arctos, all jailed for trying to break into Vane's manor to meet him.

That night [[People/Donnie|Donnie]], a [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Ghost]] and old friend, came half-translucent into his room. They spoke about the mole in the Ghosts, about the consultant [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] brought in from further down the horizon, and about a way into the party in Teller's Run. Johnny put Donnie on the trail of [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs]] and [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]], and told him he was welcome to come along if he could find a place in the car.

On Sunday he talked the Party's way to the back of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus]], first at the gate under the name Salvado Van Warhol, then to the Heart's servant, who asked how he knew [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]] and what painting he had to sell. He answered that he had a Kellum Quinn, and the servant sent them off anyway. Driving out, Benny caught their car's radio slipping itself to a dead frequency. Afterward Johnny said the museum was the next step.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|MetCon]] he looked for any Quinn on the walls and then trailed a tour group without paying, only to find the tour was Arctos's. He talked Arctos into taking the Quinn painting from [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor without asking, arguing that the host had awakened him and so everything he did was the host's will. At 414 Anchor Street he fought in the darkness, raised a false Sbrtlby out of an illusion to stab one of the pusks, and killed another of the henchmen with silver darts.

After the drug works came down he rode back to the [[Sin and Tonic]] with the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Marchal]] twins. At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] he read the Party's offer to [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]], trading the [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] *Second Meaning* for keystone 14 and for the waiving of all Prime Meridian fees, and promised the Heart any art they found. When [[Org/Concordia|Concordia]] came for the stone in the lobby, he mocked [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]] and left him clapping and laughing, and Maller never stopped.

The red choker taken off [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]] went to him: it lets its wearer speak and write the tongue of demons, and he is the one whose work is all in words.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] he and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] searched the dead and found no ID on either ranked agent. Back at the [[Sin and Tonic]] he argued against leaving keystone 14 with [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]] while mind control was loose in the city, and the Party settled on a lead-lined safe set in cement in the twins' room. He knew that lead or running water will block an ordinary locate spell, but that a pinpoint names an object and finds it anywhere, and said so.

Over downtime he taught improv classes for a few hundred gold under the name Jonathan Scaff, met the contact of the [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]], and traded on the name of the [[Org/Ghosts of Raelion|Ghosts]] to ask after bigger guns. What he learned was that the company works with a consultant named Salo Murn, who came back from a starward expedition with a little technology taken from a city he had raided, and that they cannot make high-calibre firearms until they get more. He spent the rest of the time watching [[Org/Pyrelight/index|Pyrelight]] and the Embercall, looking for a way past the wall of fire, through the sewers or otherwise, and for how the invitations to their parties are given out.

Over the six months of downtime he helped [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] try to turn the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] into something they could look at, using the papers and corkboard taken from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. He spent the rest of it looking into ways into [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], and turned up three: an invitation to the parties in the district's skyscraper, written to a named guest and carrying a 25,000 gold cover fee; a drop over the fire cordon, which the [[Org/Laity|Laity]] tried once without result; and a way under the wall through the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sewers|sewers]] or the [[Geography/Quiet Below/index|Quiet Below]].

At the [[People/Sharp the Cunning Man|Cunning Man]]'s hut he went out to a butcher and came back with two pints of goat's blood at three silver a pint, and talked Sharp into taking what was left as payment, though Sharp thought he had gotten the better of the deal. He went into the sewers with the others, lit a modern torch for the dark stretch under the river, and kept the party quiet when they neared Teller's Run.

He went back into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sewers|royal waterways]] with the others and fought the oozes, and was nearly killed by the living tar. At the far end of the long hall he took the hairline crack in the air for a smaller version of the crack in the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]] and wanted to go through it. He laid out the party's choices: walk away and return after the pilgrimage, walk away and tell someone else, or go back in and deal with it now.

In the fight in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sewers|royal waterways]] a jelly's curse aged him for a moment and left him with one gray hair.
